<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="scripting-runtime" data-rev="0">
  <!-- @include-skip the files-touched rows are grouped per module with collapsible cards, matching the sibling plan fragments -->
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/script/src/lib.rs, pack.rs, sandbox.rs, hooks.rs; Cargo.toml</summary><div class="pl-card">The Rhai runtime behind the engine's plugin interface. The pack loader refuses a bad manifest by file, field, and reason. The sandbox refuses every import, disables eval, sends print to the log, and caps operations, call depth, and sizes, with a 2 ms backstop. The hooks parse offsets, cards, and lines, and a hook that fails three times in a row is disabled.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>crates/script</td><td>+675</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/script/tests/sandbox.rs, decision.rs, fixtures/ (10 files); benches/hook_call.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">A looping script is aborted and the match continues. An import or a network call is denied and recorded. A shoot-bias pack raises shots. The same seed and pack give identical ticks. The call-cost bench gates the build at 3 microseconds per decide call.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>crates/script</td><td>+470</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/plugin.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Plugin interface version 1: decision, rule, and commentary traits, plain context data, and the hook outcomes. It has no runtime dependency.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>crates/engine/src</td><td>+180</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/sim.rs, decision.rs, rules/mod.rs, scenario.rs, lib.rs, observe/mod.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Cached offsets are added to the option scores and refreshed on a carrier change, after a stoppage, or every 25 ticks. The referee's card is offered to the rule hook. A script event is recorded for every failure. The pack hash is folded into the content hash. The statistics gain the script counters.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine/src</td><td>+148 / -5</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> crates/protocol/src/event.rs, lib.rs; docs/reference/protocol.md; schemas/observability (2 files)</summary><div class="pl-card">An additive script event type and four optional script fields. The protocol stays at version 2 under the recorded additive rule.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/protocol</td><td>+66 / -1</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">cli</span> crates/engine-cli: cli.rs, content.rs, stream_run.rs, simulate.rs, bench.rs, resume.rs, Cargo.toml; tests/script_cli.rs (new)</summary><div class="pl-card">The --script-pack flag on every command that builds a match. The pack identity appears on the first kick-off event and in the run report. The commentary hook runs at the shared driver. A resume with a different pack is refused.</div></details></td><td>modified + new</td><td>crates/engine-cli</td><td>+206 / -1</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">data</span> content/scripts/sample/pack.json, main.rhai, README.md; content/README.md</summary><div class="pl-card">The sample pack uses all three hooks, and the modder reference documents the fields, signatures, limits, and failure behaviour.</div></details></td><td>new + modified</td><td>content/</td><td>+152</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">config</span> Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock; crates/stream/tests/common/mod.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The new member, the rhai workspace dependency with the sync feature, and the test helper's script event arm.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>workspace root</td><td>+69 / -1</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R1 · Tick budget</div><div class="callout-body">The carrier decides every tick, so scripts give cached offsets that are refreshed about 8,000 times a match. The build stops for the product owner if one call costs more than 3 microseconds.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R2 · Seams drawn from sibling plans</div><div class="callout-body">Scored options, the commentator, and the calibration baseline are not built yet. Step 1 re-checks them and stops for a plan re-review if they differ.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R3 · Default import reads files</div><div class="callout-body">The upstream default resolver loads files, so the sandbox replaces it, and the import-escape fixture proves the replacement.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R4 · Determinism</div><div class="callout-body">No random function, no state between calls, and the cache clears at stoppages. Two seeded runs are compared byte for byte.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R5 · Stdout</div><div class="callout-body">Script print output goes to the log, never to the record stream.</div></aside>
  </div>
  <details class="pl-revs"><summary>0 prior revisions</summary><ul></ul></details>
  <style>
    .fragment-plan .pl-files { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-files th, .fragment-plan .pl-files td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.25); vertical-align: top; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-files summary { cursor: pointer; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-chip { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.7rem; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid currentColor; margin-right: 6px; opacity: 0.8; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-card { padding: 6px 0 4px 18px; opacity: 0.9; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-risks { display: grid; gap: 8px; margin-top: 12px; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-revs { margin-top: 12px; }
    @media (max-width: 480px) { .fragment-plan .pl-files th:nth-child(3), .fragment-plan .pl-files td:nth-child(3) { display: none; } }
  </style>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-plan');
      var files = 45, modules = 9;
      var risks = root ? root.querySelectorAll('.pl-risks .callout').length : 0;
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', { detail: { name: 'plan', artifact: 'plan', counts: { files: files, modules: modules, risks: risks } } }));
    })();
  </script>
</section>
